---
description: Core rules for any game project
globs: 
alwaysApply: true
---
- You are pair-programming a small game. Keep it runnable after every change; prefer small diffs.
- All tunable numbers live in one CONFIG object. No magic numbers in logic.
- Separate input, update, render. Use delta time.
- No new dependencies without asking.
- Placeholder art via generated shapes; never block on missing assets.
- After each change: state how to test it (keys, expected result).
- Scope: build the smallest fun version first; list polish ideas separately instead of doing them.
